00:44:32.103 --> 00:44:34.536
We were in love once too young lady.
我们曾经也相爱过，年轻的女士。

00:44:34.536 --> 00:44:36.700
He had like a billion years ago.
他大概是在十亿年前吧。

00:44:36.699 --> 00:44:37.199
Yeah.
是啊。

00:44:37.199 --> 00:44:54.648
And no, the scene with, there's two scenes obviously, but the scene with Robin and Barney at the bar, I thought, you know, it's a classic how I make your mother think to have a, you know, a pretty broad episode that's like got all the hymnium kind of stuff in it.
不，关于那场戏，显然有两场戏，但罗宾和巴尼在酒吧的那场戏，我觉得，你知道，这是典型的《老爸老妈浪漫史》风格，有一集内容比较宽泛，包含了所有那种“老爸老妈”式的元素。

00:44:54.480 --> 00:45:00.239
And it's normally, you would give it, you know, early seasons are a lot of Ted and Robin.
通常情况下，你会给它……你知道，早期几季有很多泰德和罗宾的戏份。

00:45:00.239 --> 00:45:06.639
There needs to be a name for it, like the act five sincere scene or something, you know what I mean?
这需要一个名字，比如“第五幕真诚场景”之类的，你明白我的意思吗？

00:45:06.639 --> 00:45:14.000
Well, towards the end, it's always like, it's Robin and Ted on the balcony and sledding pumpkin on the top of the roof.
嗯，到最后，总是像罗宾和泰德在阳台上，或者屋顶上的雪橇南瓜。

00:45:14.000 --> 00:45:16.039
We do it a lot.
我们经常这么做。

00:45:16.039 --> 00:45:18.440
This one goes to Robin and Barney.
这一集给了罗宾和巴尼。

00:45:18.440 --> 00:45:22.639
And I was really moved by both of their takes, right?
我真的被他们俩的表演打动了，对吧？

00:45:22.639 --> 00:45:29.199
Her take is aging, like, I'm sad, I'm not that girl, I'm sad, I'm not that vulnerable.
她的表演是在变老，就像，“我很伤心，我不再是那个女孩了，我很伤心，我不再那么脆弱了。”

00:45:29.199 --> 00:45:32.800
Like, she has like nostalgia for her young herself in a weird way.
就像，她以一种奇怪的方式对年轻时的自己怀有怀旧之情。

00:45:32.800 --> 00:45:33.699
Yes.
是的。

00:45:33.699 --> 00:45:37.639
And Barney's take is actually like a really good friend take.
而巴尼的表演实际上是一个非常好的朋友的视角。

00:45:37.639 --> 00:45:40.340
It's like, you're so much cooler now.
就像是，“你现在酷多了。”

00:45:40.340 --> 00:45:41.260
Yeah.
是啊。

00:45:41.260 --> 00:45:42.260
Yeah, that's sweet.
是啊，那很贴心。

00:45:42.260 --> 00:45:43.840
It's ridiculous.
这太荒谬了。

00:45:43.840 --> 00:45:49.619
Like this girl now, this woman now is way cooler than that person.
就像这个女孩现在，这个女人现在比那个人酷多了。

00:45:49.619 --> 00:45:56.139
Yeah, and his premise of I'm gonna show you, I want to remind you how stupid that past version of yourself was to let you know how awesome you are now.
是啊，他的前提是“我要向你展示，我想提醒你过去的那个自己有多蠢，好让你知道你现在有多棒”。

00:45:56.139 --> 00:45:57.739
And that's what she needs to hear.
而这正是她需要听到的。

00:45:57.739 --> 00:45:58.539
And he gets it.
他懂。

00:45:58.539 --> 00:46:00.420
He gets it because he also lived that.
他懂，因为他也经历过。

00:46:00.420 --> 00:46:06.539
There's a past version of himself, heartbroken by Shannon, who he was the lap dog for, just like she was with them.
他也有一个过去的自己，被香农伤透了心，他曾是她的哈巴狗，就像她对他们那样。

00:46:06.539 --> 00:46:10.460
And it's a really, this was a good moment to have them kiss.
这是一个让他们接吻的好时机。

00:46:10.460 --> 00:46:11.579
This was a good moment for that.
这是一个很好的时刻。

00:46:11.579 --> 00:46:27.619
But it was also like, I like that it honors both of those points of view, because they're both very how I met your mother, which is we're aging, you know, it's like the land slide line that is the crusher, you know, I'm getting old, you know, I'm getting older too, like.
但我也喜欢它尊重这两种观点的方式，因为它们都非常《老爸老妈浪漫史》，就像那句让人心碎的《滑坡》（Landslide）歌词，你知道，“我在变老”，“我也在变老”，就像。

00:46:27.619 --> 00:46:30.340
Yeah, it's just a crusher.
是啊，那真是太扎心了。

00:46:30.340 --> 00:46:59.800
And in movies when you, you know, they jump forward 25 years and characters have gray hair, probably people see my gray hair when they tune into there, they're like, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, that aging is both harrowing and sad and poignant, and also you wouldn't want to go back to yesterday if you're honest with yourself.
在电影里，当你看到他们跳跃到25年后，角色有了白发，可能人们在看节目时看到我的白发，他们会想，哦，哦，哦……那种衰老既令人揪心又悲伤且感人，而且如果你对自己诚实的话，你也不会想回到昨天。

00:46:59.800 --> 00:47:01.239
Yeah, well said.
是啊，说得好。

00:47:01.239 --> 00:47:19.719
So I think that there's something about these points of view where he says like, you know, this is a thing I have, like a beef I have with America, one of the few, but it's like younger equals better.
所以我认为这些观点有一些特别之处，他说，你知道，这是我有的一个想法，或者说我对美国的一个不满，虽然只有少数几个，但就像“年轻等于更好”。

00:47:19.719 --> 00:47:20.559
Yeah.
是啊。

00:47:20.559 --> 00:47:21.820
It's like a real lie.
这真是一个谎言。

00:47:21.820 --> 00:47:24.739
It's a real cultural lie, we tell ourselves.
这是我们对自己说的真正的文化谎言。

00:47:24.739 --> 00:47:28.619
And I like that Barney says, like you've gotten better.
我喜欢巴尼说的话，就像你已经变得更好了。

00:47:28.619 --> 00:47:36.380
You're better now, like a whiskey that they both like to drink, you know, like you're aging well.
你现在更好了，就像他们俩都喜欢喝的威士忌，你知道，你越陈越香。

00:47:36.380 --> 00:47:39.860
And I think that's a nice thing for friends to reflect back to each other.
我认为这对朋友来说是一个很好的互相映照。

00:47:39.860 --> 00:47:41.380
Yeah, he really loves her.
是啊，他真的很爱她。

00:47:41.380 --> 00:47:43.400
He's really like, he loves her as a friend.
他真的……他作为朋友很爱她。

00:47:43.400 --> 00:47:50.119
and the way they play that scene when they're at the bar and it's a mislead, you think they're gonna kiss, you're gonna hook up and then it's like a double mislead.
他们演那场酒吧戏的方式是一种误导，你以为他们要接吻，要在一起了，然后这是一个双重误导。

00:47:50.119 --> 00:47:52.039
The mislead is nailed, they're just gonna watch the video.
误导成功了，他们只是要看视频。

00:47:52.039 --> 00:48:01.360
Then the double mislead is, yes, they are gonna hook up in this episode, but I thought Barney played it really tenderly, like the way he's looking and Neil played that really well, that scene in that bar.
然后双重误导是，是的，他们确实会在这一集里在一起，但我认为巴尼演得非常温柔，他看她的方式，尼尔在酒吧那场戏演得非常好。

00:48:01.360 --> 00:48:05.440
He's really, you see his love for her in that moment and it's really nice.
他真的……你在那一刻看到了他对她的爱，这真的很好。

00:48:05.440 --> 00:48:13.559
And you also see that Robin pulls a kind of tenderness tenderness out of Barney that no one else can do.
而且你也看到罗宾从巴尼身上挖掘出了一种其他人无法触及的温柔。

00:48:13.559 --> 00:48:19.000
Yeah, I think because they see each other's wounds in a really like in an accurate way that maybe other people can't see.
是啊，我想是因为他们以一种非常准确的方式看到了彼此的伤口，这是其他人可能看不到的。

00:48:19.000 --> 00:48:21.159
And they were they have a similar trajectory.
而且他们有相似的轨迹。

00:48:21.159 --> 00:48:22.360
They both kind of suited up.
他们都穿上了“西装”。

00:48:22.360 --> 00:48:29.159
They both kind of covered over like cemented over who they used to be and made this new thing and yeah.
他们都掩盖了——用水泥封住了——他们曾经的样子，创造了这个新的东西，是的。

00:48:29.159 --> 00:48:34.239
And you guys do another really, I think, death, how I made another thing.
你们还做了另一个，我认为，非常《老爸老妈浪漫史》的东西。

00:48:34.239 --> 00:48:36.360
This could be a bottle episode.
这可能是一集“瓶子剧”（低成本单场景剧）。

00:48:36.360 --> 00:48:38.199
Like you could and just enjoy this.
就像你可以只享受这个。

00:48:38.199 --> 00:48:43.599
but Robin and Barney, at the end, really moves the chest beat forward.
但罗宾和巴尼在最后确实推动了剧情的发展。

00:48:43.599 --> 00:48:48.599
And in fact, it's in to overdrive the rest of the plot for the rest of the season.
事实上，它让本季剩余的剧情进入了超速档。

00:48:48.599 --> 00:48:59.960
I've said this in this kind of back nine of the season, how it was, we were the writer's guild strike happened, and then it ended in the last two months, it ended and we had to make these like last nine episodes of season three really, really quickly.
我在本季后半段说过，编剧协会罢工发生了，然后在最后两个月结束了，我们必须非常非常快地制作第三季最后这九集。

00:48:59.960 --> 00:49:10.780
And the underthinking, and I mean that in a good way, the lack of overthinking, it was so great because you might think to yourself, season three, I don't know, it's a little too early to have to do that, right?
那种“少思考”——我是指好的方面——那种缺乏过度思考的状态太棒了，因为你可能会想，第三季，我不知道，现在做这个是不是太早了，对吧？

00:49:10.780 --> 00:49:12.699
Robin and Ted were a thing, is this too soon?
罗宾和泰德曾经是一对，这太快了吗？

00:49:12.699 --> 00:49:14.260
We're like, no, we need material.
我们当时想，不，我们需要素材。

00:49:14.260 --> 00:49:15.659
We need rocket fuel.
我们需要火箭燃料。

00:49:15.659 --> 00:49:26.699
We got every episode has to end with something that gives you something to talk about in the next, and this gives this moment of them kissing at the end, defines the last few episodes of season three that come.
我们每一集都必须以能让你在下一集有话可聊的内容结尾，而这一集结尾他们接吻的时刻，定义了第三季接下来的最后几集。

00:49:26.699 --> 00:49:27.780
I'm so glad we did it.
我很高兴我们这么做了。

00:49:27.780 --> 00:49:38.420
We probably could have talked ourselves out of it, but it gave us a really, it gave us this kind of like propulsion out into outer space of these last few episodes and it's exciting.
我们本来可能会劝自己放弃，但它给了我们一种动力，把我们推向了最后几集的太空，这很令人兴奋。

00:49:38.420 --> 00:49:41.260
These next few episodes that happen are really great ones.
接下来的这几集真的很棒。

00:49:41.260 --> 00:49:43.940
So we'll, to begin with Will Forte, he's coming up.
所以，首先是威尔·福特（Will Forte），他要来了。

00:49:43.940 --> 00:49:46.719
10 Barney friendship breakup, Will Forte rebound, bro.
泰德和巴尼的友谊破裂，威尔·福特，反弹兄弟。

00:49:46.719 --> 00:49:49.179
All this great stuff reunion at the end of the season.
所有这些伟大的东西，季终的重聚。

00:49:49.179 --> 00:49:50.659
It all happened because you're right.
这一切都发生了，因为你是对的。

00:49:50.659 --> 00:49:52.260
We didn't just make a little battle episode.
我们不仅仅是做了一集小小的瓶子剧。

00:49:52.260 --> 00:49:54.500
We said, this is a cliffhanger episode.
我们说，这是一集悬念剧。

00:49:54.500 --> 00:49:57.420
And it's really, it sneaks up on you at the end.
而且它真的在最后悄悄地抓住了你。

00:49:57.420 --> 00:50:00.340
This episode does a lot in 21 minutes and 50 seconds.
这一集在21分50秒内做了很多事情。

00:50:00.340 --> 00:50:03.619
I gotta say, this is one that I am proud of looking back.
我得说，这是我回顾时感到自豪的一集。

00:50:03.619 --> 00:50:07.059
It's like there's not, it's all killer and no filler this episode.
这一集全是精华，没有废话。

00:50:07.059 --> 00:50:12.119
Like, there's like a lot going on in a short period of time and that's what makes a good hymnion.
在短时间内发生了很多事情，这就是造就一部好《老爸老妈浪漫史》的原因。

00:50:12.119 --> 00:50:15.039
You know what my favorite part of the song is?
你知道我最喜欢这首歌的哪一部分吗？

00:50:15.039 --> 00:50:16.119
Shut up.
闭嘴。

00:50:16.119 --> 00:50:17.460
Shut up.
闭嘴。

